														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4863119">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Normal</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The Foundation's objective is to preserve normalcy, and it stops at that, what about the average people, the people with no connection with the abnormal, caught in the crossfire between different GOIs, SCPs, and end up on the Foundation's casualty report. This SCP aims to somewhat alleviate that. A series of instructions, warnings, one-time-use spells, etc, etc given to the victims of these anomalous incidents (just a portion of them, enough to catch the Foundation's attention) to help them escape the situation unharmed. but the reality is often bleaker than it looks.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> We are presented with the SCP, the set of requirements for its manifestation. Then, we look through the list of incidents it took place in (about 8 ~ 15 I haven't found the goldilocks number to form a pattern or a narrative yet, officially in the record, it would be around a few thousand). The pattern we see here would be that this SCP has pretty much about 35% success rate with success being the receiver will have no other connection with the anomaly and survive(of course) the rest would be either dead (anomalously or not), sunk deeper into the abnormal, recruited by different GOIs (including the Foundation). Then we are presented with some transcript of the SCP's instruction and we would see some changes in tones, sadder, more pessimistic, although more professional, a stand out transcript would show why it did what it did.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The audience would be hooked (hopefully) with the question of &quot;What about the average civilian in the world dwelled within the anomaly?&quot; and the methods that this unknown force behind the SCP utilizes to help the victims and how the Foundation apply them to standard protocols. Then, hopefully, the audience would see how this kind of work affects an individual, people become more jaded but also more proficient at what they do.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> This SCP might be a more primitive + anomalous version of 911 operatives (now I've just realized that&#8230;) but instead of you finding their help, they will try to help you. This is my first idea on the site, so a bit nervous, a lot actually. Hope you like it. If not, all criticism is welcomed.</p>

							</div>

								
					
